{"availability":"available","full":"fly-pigTH/EquiMus","name":"EquiMus","description":"A MuJoCo-based framework for energy-equivalent modeling and simulation of musculoskeletal robots.","category":"Education","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":82,"forks":1,"created":"2025-10-07T05:12:45Z","updated":"2026-03-19T02:14:06Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fly-pigth.github.io/EquiMus.github.io/","topics":["algorithms","control","framework","ieee","learning","muscle","musculoskeletal-simulations","reinforcement-learning","robot","robotics","simluation","soft","softrobot","softrobotics","software"],"demo":"https://fly-pigth.github.io/EquiMus.github.io/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.872Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.872Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.872Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:17.872Z","stars":82,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["EquiMus is an energy-equivalent dynamic modeling framework that brings musculoskeletal robots into real-time simulation, based on MuJoCo. It converts soft actuators (e.g., pneumatic muscles, FEAs) into a rigorously derived 3-2-1 lumped-mass representation, preserving their true kinetic, potential, damping, and actuation energies.","This allows EquiMus to accurately model dynamic mass redistribution, biarticular routing, and kinematic loops within standard MuJoCo workflows—features that are traditionally hard (or impossible) to simulate.","👉 In short: EquiMus makes muscle-driven robots truly simulatable."],"features":["EquiMus: Musculoskeletal Equivalent Dynamic Modeling and Simulation for Rigid-soft Hybrid Robots with Linear Elastic Actuators","💡 What Problems Does EquiMus Solve?","🎶 Design Philosophy","🚀 Install \\& Run EquiMus (3 minutes)","📂 Project Structure"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/fly-pigTH/EquiMus/blob/main/readme.md","fingerprint":"822beaef972f5015a3e12bf71a5c4b550dcbb74a8a4431beceb93